<!--Post: 12700--><!--Time: 1112855261-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12700"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 06, 2005 - 11:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another &#34;Victor Special&#34;: <BR> <BR>This one is for any theories on how to PREVENT FUTURE BTKs. Any ideas whatsoever on STOPPING serial killers BEFORE they ever get started. What a concept, huh? <BR> <BR>IS there any way of keeping those vile humans from ever acting out on their serial killing impulses in the first place? <BR> <BR>Stay tuned here &amp; find out........<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12700-->
<!--Post: 12704--><!--Time: 1112881060-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12704"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 6:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->V: <BR> <BR>I don’t think you can. <BR> <BR>First, the incidence of psychopaths in the general population is quite high.  The leading contemporary authority on psychopaths, Robert Hare, estimates one in a hundred north americans is a psychopath.  <a href="http://news.bbc.co.uk/1/hi/northern_ireland/4057771.stm" target=_top>http://news.bbc.co.uk/1/hi/northern_ireland/405777 1.stm</a>.  The psychopathic personality has sub-types, one of which is the sexual psychopath. Serial Killers are sexual psychopaths. <BR> <BR>Second, even though we have had a description of the disorder since 1886,&#40;Richard von Krafft-Ebbing, Pscyhopathia Sexualis&#41;, we have yet to identify a cause.  Hare&#39;s book &#34;Without Conscience. The Disturbing World of the Psychopaths Among Us&#34; argues that psychopaths are born not made.  There is no causal connection between child abuse and psychopaths. <BR> <BR>With all this in mind, I don&#39;t think you can stop them before they get started because the act of killing is a diagnostic event.  In other words, you know you&#39;re dealing with a sexual psychopath because they kill. <BR> <BR>Someone who has never killed anyone is not a serial killer. <BR> <BR>Phoenix <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12704-->
<!--Post: 12706--><!--Time: 1112884932-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12706"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 7:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Should we ever know the life spectrum of Rader, one might be able to tell in hind sight what may have contributed to his BTK career. He clearly has a strong resentment toward a female figure, substituting numerous women for her. Some male in his past family  disrepected females in front of Rader. Somehow he associated sexual excitement and pain at a young age.  <BR> <BR>I do not think that serial killers can be prevented. Everyone in the world would have to be in therapy before the terrible two&#39;s. Somewhere in everyone&#39;s life is a very bitter experience, probably not even consciously remembered by the person, that has changed how they interpret life&#39;s events. Some recoil from the world in horror, some fight back, and some just freeze. You can be assured that his mother is spending many sleepless nights wondering what she did that made him BTK. If not, that may be part of the answer as to his character. Family secrets, family shame: the shame and blame of child rearing practices during his childhood and youth has had a untoward effect on baby boomers, of which I am one. His life in church created a facade instead of a change in heart. Somewhere between physiology, childhood experiences, and the spiritual history of his family lies only part of the answer. Within the last 4 generations of his family, with him being the fourth, is a male who behaved very similarly to Rader. I would make book on it. <BR> <BR>Was the sadism practiced on him as a child? Did someone tie him up as a &#39;lesson&#39; and then shame him when he wet his pants because he could not hold it until he was untied? He has shown someone that he can take what was dished out to him and he can give it back in spades.  <BR> <BR>This is a great thread for everyone to speculate &#39;what went wrong with Rader?&#39;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12706-->
<!--Post: 12707--><!--Time: 1112886554-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12707"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 8:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think a good start would be to catch them and punish them all in a span of less time than would allow them to live out their golden years on a serial killer&#39;s 401k program.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12707-->
<!--Post: 12709--><!--Time: 1112887012-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12709"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 8:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is no preventing such a phenomenon, truly. Any efforts based on the current thinking about what produces serial killers would result in over-control and over-regulation of people&#39;s personal lives to a fascist degree. There are, oddly, more people out there than we realize who mentally are very close to being one, but they simply never make the leap into homicide - so in essence, there&#39;s no real answer to your question. Sadly, we know that once they start, there&#39;s no curing them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12709-->
<!--Post: 12714--><!--Time: 1112898637-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12714"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lizzie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lizzie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 11:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I would like to see them stopped quicker once they start. It seems like if there was a way to database things like MO, victim similarities, DNA, fingerprints, composite skectes, etc. internationally or at the least countrywide, similarities to other cases might be found that could help catch the next BTK sooner. A combination of techniques used by people at this board as well as handwriting analysis and de-coding tools might also help find the criminals sooner that communicate with LE or the public.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12714-->
<!--Post: 12716--><!--Time: 1112900644-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12716"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 12:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->P’x <BR> <BR>I always enjoy your postings. <BR> <BR>About that one percent... <BR> <BR>Have you read “The Sociopath Next Door” by Martha Stout? <BR> <BR>I’ve only read about the book. <BR> <BR>Apparently, Stout estimates that four percent of North Americans live with a disorder which robs them of compassion, conscience and shame. <BR>These are people who may be gifted with charisma but are totally devoid of the ability to love. <BR> <BR>Four percent! I was aghast. <BR> <BR>Then I started to ponder my sphere of influence. <BR>I imagined a room full of two-hundred good friends and acquaintances, neighbors, colleagues, ex-girlfriends, clients and relatives. <BR> <BR>It didn’t take long to come up with – <BR> <BR>one cold-blooded murderer - - Jane, I still can’t believe you got away with it! <BR>three registered sex offenders &#40;one makes his living as a locksmith&#41; <BR>four more child molesters &#40;ES&amp;D cousin Marc&#41; <BR>Kelly, the wife-abusing, home-wrecking, gambling-and-alcohol-addicted, tax-evading, life-of-the-party who pilfered his parent’s life savings <BR>Father John, who came to the house frequently - - before being defrocked for impregnating a teenage girl and subsequently paying for her abortion <BR>don’t get me started on my brother-in-law – poor devil <BR> <BR>For those of you keeping score at home, that makes eleven. <BR>Granted, I do know more than 200 people. <BR>However, eight of those mentioned above have dwelled in my core circle of acquaintances – and… <BR>I only spent five minutes making my list. <BR>I know I could come up with more and the clever ones will go undetected. <BR> <BR>Steve Huff is correct. <BR>A totalitarian government could diagnose and exterminate sociopaths with efficiency. <BR>Of course, the historical models show that this kind of leadership tends to instill psychopathic behavior among the citizenry. <BR>Think about this. “Good Germans” were made… not born. <BR> <BR>Here’s some questions for all y’all: <BR> <BR>Why does a truly free society, one based on the principles of fair play, equality and Judeo-Christian ethics seem to cough up more than it’s fair share of monsters? <BR> <BR>What is it that drives us to such violence?  <BR>There is an ongoing price to pay for our freedom to express, no? <BR>Do the military, legislative and societal battles fought to preserve, protect and spread the freedoms we cherish, leave a dastardly residue that must be recognized and accepted?  <BR> <BR>I have more thoughts on the subject, but as some of you are already sensing – I’m in way over my head. <BR> <BR>LayDog  <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12716-->
<!--Post: 12718--><!--Time: 1112915694-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12718"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 4:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Serial killers have nothing to do with the freedoms or lack of freedoms from where they come. <BR>They know no religious, ethnic or geographical boundries and they know no social class. <BR>Under the oppressive Czarist and Soviet governments of Russia cam at least 11 searial killers from the 1880&#39;s to the 1990&#39;s that claimed more than 700 victims. <BR>The Soviet block countries of Belarus, Czrch Republic, Hungary, Romania, Ukraine, Yougoslavia and Poland all had multiple serial killers in the 20th century. <BR>China has had serial killers. <BR>The far east of Japan, Korea, Thailand, Taiwan and Indonesia have had serial killers. <BR>India has had serial killers. <BR>The Islamic nations of Pakistan, Jordan, United Arab Emirates, Yemen and Egypt have had serial killers. <BR>Every Scandanavian nation including Sweden, Norway, Denmark and Finland have had serial killers. <BR>The European nations of England, Ireland, France, Germany, Austria, Belgium, Greece, Spain, Estonia and the Netherlands have all had serial killers. <BR>The tiny, nuetral, peace-loving country of Switzerland has had at least four serail killers between the 1880&#39;s and the 1980&#39;s. <BR>A new country was created in the mid 20th century. They called it Israel and within five years of it&#39;s birth they had a serial killer. <BR>In this hemisphere south of the American border in Mexico, Nicaragua, Bolivia, Columbia, Guetamala, El Salvador, Peru and Columbia you will find the stories of each of those nations multiple serial killers. <BR>It&#39;s enough to make you want to get away from it all. Well forget the Bahamas because they&#39;ve had at least one serial killer in Nassau. <BR> How about our peaceful remote sparsely populated neighbors to the north, Canada? Not very likely you&#39;ll run into a serial killer there. Wrong. They have had at least 27 during the 20th century alone.  <BR>If you come up with a formula for stopping serial killers before they start thus eliminating all global serial killing you will be the recipient of the Nobel Prize in a couple of categories and be given audiences before presidents, kings, sultans, swamis, dictators and popes. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12718-->
<!--Post: 12719--><!--Time: 1112925353-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12719"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 6:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It would be difficult to prevent future serial murderers. Most serial murderers are psychopaths, but not all psychopaths become serial murderers. The typical serial murderer does not exist. One may be motivated by hatred towards his mother, another may hate a former girlfriend or wife and another may murder to compensate for his inability to experience a romantic relationship with a woman. <BR> <BR>Psychiatrists have failed to diagnose potential serial murderers in the past. Ed Kemper visited his psychiatrist a day after he murdered Aikoo Koo. The psychiatrist evaluated his mental health and reached the conclusion Kemper was no longer a danger to himself or others and recommended his juvenile record be sealed. Kemper was diagnosed as a personality trait disturbance, passive-aggressive type at Atascadero State hospital in California. He was committed to the hospital for murdering his grandparents at the age of 15. State psychiatrists objected to his 1969 release from the hospital. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12719-->
<!--Post: 12721--><!--Time: 1112927676-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12721"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 7:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jo, <BR> <BR>Very interesting and very scary. <BR>I&#39;ll say it again; the behavior spreads like a virus. <BR> <BR>I have heard the Ukraine called the &#34;serial killer capital of the world&#34;. <BR>Do they own the per capita statistic Johno? <BR> <BR>Civil war and the dysfunction that it breeds is a nasty catalyst. <BR>One would think that El Salvador, Nicaragua or Rwanda would be a hotbed for insatiable bloodlust. <BR> <BR>I suppose my impression is that we seem to have more psycho killers per capita here in the U.S.A. <BR> <BR>Do we?... or are we just more efficient at identifying and reporting the phenomena? <BR> <BR>If we do lead the world in fostering lone human hunters, why is it so? <BR> <BR>LD <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12721-->
<!--Post: 12723--><!--Time: 1112931352-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12723"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 8:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Parents: PAY ATTENTION to your children!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
